* START-HISTORY:
* 3 Nov 26 dm  New (S.130; the owner: "Public wrapper library").
* END-HISTORY
*
* START-DESCRIPTION:
*
*   call !tkopen(app, ctx, err, floorw, floorh)           ALWAYS FIVE ARGUMENTS: a call with fewer stops with "Argument count mismatch" (pad with '')
*
*     app       the program's name, for the messages and the right end of row 0
*     ctx       returned: the context (tkpub.h) every other !tk routine is given
*     err       returned: null when the program may go on; else the message to print (the program prints it and stops).  Nothing has been drawn
*     floorw floorh   the smallest window the program is laid out for; null for 140 by 43, the smallest a floor may be is 100 by 30
*
*   THE AUDIENCE IS ALWAYS THE USER'S: $tk_open is asked for a page of the person's own (the right end of row 0 says "name@account") and never for an administrator page, so
*   this library cannot open one.  It runs with the rights and the gates of the session that calls it: it adds none, and every file the program opens is opened by the program.
*   Give the screen back with !tkclose on EVERY way out.
*
* END-DESCRIPTION
*
* START-CODE

$internal
subroutine tkopen(app, ctx, err, floorw, floorh)
$catalog !tkopen

   call $tk_open(app, '', ctx, err, floorw, floorh)
   return
end

* END-CODE
